  abstract = {Providing a proof certificate is one of the most important features of (fully automated) theorem proving systems. For theorem provers based on, e.g, resolution or superposition calculi, a syntax for writing solutions is well documented and used. Even though attempts have been made to specify a syntax for connection calculi, there is currently no such syntax in common use. This paper provides an overview of the proof syntax used by existing connection provers and proposes an improved syntax for connection proofs. Due to the general approach, the syntax can be extended to also represent connection proofs in some non-classical logics.},
